<h3 class="wp-block-heading tf-cell__h">A Table for Eight</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"tf-cell__txt"} -->
<p class="tf-cell__txt">On a rainy October evening in Aldmere, a family gathered to celebrate an anniversary dinner around a wooden dining table. Tomás Reyes designed a low arrangement in an aged copper bowl, using garden roses, late ranunculus, and wild autumn foliage gathered from regional growers. Kept deliberately low so that guests could see and converse without obstruction, the flowers caught the candlelight, bringing warm earth tones, delicate fragrance, and a sense of relaxed celebration to an eight-person feast that lasted well into the night.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"tf-tags tf-tags--l"} -->
<p class="tf-tags tf-tags--l">#anniversary #lowtable</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"tf-cell tf-cell--text","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
